<Base
  title={'eInvoicing transformation case study — Felipe Alves'}
  description={'Programme reporting, data integration and status standardisation for a current Finance eInvoicing transformation spanning 40+ applications.'}
  ogDescription={'Reporting, data integration and status standardisation across a 40+ application Finance transformation.'}
  ogType="article"
  css={['styles', 'responsive', 'enhancements', 'site-fixes', 'illustrations']}
  bodyClass="case-page"
  script="script"
>
<main><section class="case-hero section-shell reveal"><div><span class="status-pill">Current · in progress</span><span class="eyebrow" style="display:block;margin-top:18px">Case study 04 · Finance transformation</span><h1>Making a 40+ application transformation visible.</h1><p>Programme reporting, data integration and status standardisation for a Finance eInvoicing transformation spanning more than 40 impacted applications.</p></div><div class="case-facts"><div><span>Role</span><strong>Finance Data Analytics Specialist</strong></div><div><span>Scope</span><strong>40+ applications</strong></div><div><span>Focus</span><strong>SIT · UAT · integration visibility</strong></div><div><span>Sources</span><strong>QMetry · Jira · SharePoint · enterprise data</strong></div></div></section><section class="case-body section-shell"><aside class="case-nav"><a href="#context">Context</a><a href="#problem">Problem</a><a href="#approach">Approach</a><a href="#illustration">Illustration</a><a href="#limits">Disclosure boundary</a><a href="#public-context">Public context</a><a href="#reflection">Reflection</a><a class="back-link" href="/#work">← Back to work</a></aside><div><section class="case-section" id="context"><span class="eyebrow">Context</span><h2>Large transformations fail quietly when status means different things to different teams.</h2><p>The eInvoicing programme affects a broad application landscape. My role sits on the visibility layer: combine programme data, define consistent status logic and help Finance and technology stakeholders understand where testing and integration actually stand.</p></section><section class="case-section" id="problem"><span class="eyebrow">Problem</span><h2>Forty applications can create forty versions of “on track”.</h2><p>Different applications, testing phases and source systems naturally produce inconsistent status definitions. Reporting becomes useful only when the underlying terms, dates and counts mean the same thing across the programme.</p><blockquote>The data problem is not just collecting status. It is defining what status means.</blockquote></section><section class="case-section" id="approach"><span class="eyebrow">Approach</span><h2>Standardise the language before polishing the dashboard.</h2><div class="decision-grid"><div class="decision-card"><span>1</span><h3>Integrate</h3><p>Bring together test and delivery information from QMetry, Jira, SharePoint and other enterprise sources.</p></div><div class="decision-card"><span>2</span><h3>Define</h3><p>Standardise KPI definitions, testing phases, dates and status methodology so reporting is comparable.</p></div><div class="decision-card"><span>3</span><h3>Investigate</h3><p>Trace reporting inconsistencies and data-quality issues back to their source rather than masking them in presentation logic.</p></div><div class="decision-card"><span>4</span><h3>Communicate</h3><p>Turn the resulting data into decision-ready programme visibility for Finance and technology stakeholders.</p></div></div></section><StatusMappingIllustration /><section class="case-section" id="limits"><span class="eyebrow">Disclosure boundary</span><h2>What I can say — and what I deliberately do not.</h2><div class="disclosure-box"><h3>Publicly safe</h3><p>My role, the 40+ application scale, reporting/data-integration focus, SIT/UAT/integration monitoring, and the enterprise tools used for programme visibility.</p></div><div class="disclosure-box"><h3>Not represented here</h3><p>Internal architecture, vendor decisions, application-level implementation details, tax positions, delivery decisions, or whether Emirates is part of the UAE government's formal pilot cohort.</p></div></section><section class="case-section public-context" id="public-context"><span class="eyebrow">Independent public context</span><h2>The national programme entered pilot phase in July 2026.</h2><p class="context-intro">The UAE Ministry of Finance states that Electronic Invoicing commenced with a pilot programme on 1 July 2026, followed by phased mandatory implementation. My work is presented as enterprise readiness and transformation reporting in that national context.</p><div class="source-grid"><a class="source-card" href="https://mof.gov.ae/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/UAE-Electronic-Invoicing-Guidelines_V-1.1-01June2026.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span class="source-type">UAE Ministry of Finance · 2026</span><strong>Pilot from 1 July 2026</strong><span>Official Electronic Invoicing Guidelines v1.1 ↗</span></a><a class="source-card" href="https://mof.gov.ae/en/about-us/initiatives/einvoicing/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span class="source-type">National programme</span><strong>Structured B2B / B2G eInvoicing</strong><span>Programme scope and official updates ↗</span></a></div><p class="context-note">This case is intentionally lighter than the completed cases because the programme is current and much of the implementation detail is not appropriate for a public portfolio.</p></section><section class="case-section" id="reflection"><span class="eyebrow">Reflection</span><h2>Transformation reporting is a product when people use it to decide where to intervene.</h2><p>The useful part is not a colourful status page. It is the shared logic underneath it: definitions, data lineage and enough consistency that a programme lead can trust what “red”, “complete” or “ready” actually means.</p></section><section class="case-cta"><span class="eyebrow">Next</span><h2>Want to talk this through?</h2><div class="closing-actions"><a class="button primary" href="mailto:felipe.s.alves7@gmail.com">Email Felipe</a><a class="button ghost" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/felipealves7" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a><a class="button ghost" href="/#work">More selected work</a></div></section></div></section></main>
</Base>
